; The schedules live in one file that `main.bean` does NOT include, so the
; series never inflates the ledger's balances. Each schedule is a real
; Beancount transaction carrying an `id` and an `rrule`; its date is the
; schedule's next occurrence and is advanced by `beanschedule reconcile`.
;
; The plugin validates this file by path and the Fava report reconciles it. A
; schedule's other-side postings carry the split, each with its own metadata.

2026-02-15 * "Acme" "Paycheck" #payroll ^acme-2026
  id: "paycheck"
  rrule: "FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15"
  match-payee: "Acme"
  category: "income"
  amount-tolerance: 7.50
  Assets:Bank:Checking       -3000.00 USD
  Expenses:Taxes:Federal       600.00 USD
    narration: "Federal withholding"
  Expenses:Savings            2400.00 USD
    narration: "Savings transfer"
